                <pb facs="0637" n="517" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg517"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">723.2515/1082: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Collier</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-11-29T22:00:00-04:42"><hi rendition="#italic">November 29,
                                1922—10 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 11:45
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>91. My telegram number 90, November 28, 10 p.m. Protocol ratified without
                    reservations by Chilean Congress in consequence of failure of Senate this
                    afternoon to obtain more than 15 votes for reservations, 14 opposed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Collier</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
